WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:05.667
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:06.883
I am seven.

00:00:06.883 --> 00:00:10.461
Everyday before school,
I turn on the TV and

00:00:10.461 --> 00:00:14.243
watch my favorite science show for
children.

00:00:14.243 --> 00:00:18.411
It is nerdy and science and marvelous,
there are colors and bubbles and

00:00:18.411 --> 00:00:20.740
explosions, I love it.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.411
Now one day before school,
I turn on the TV,

00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:28.957
it's not playing, very weird.

00:00:28.957 --> 00:00:32.241
Day two, same thing.

00:00:32.241 --> 00:00:35.710
Mommy, what's happening?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.669
My mom tells me that
the show's been moved,

00:00:42.669 --> 00:00:46.990
it now plays when I'm in school.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:55.410
Why would you play a children's
show when children are in school?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.100
How dare you?

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.960
Adults are so stupid.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.554
My mom says chill, bro chill.

00:01:05.554 --> 00:01:09.750
She says that I should write
a letter to the TV channel.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.900
She doesn't think I'd write the letter.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.850
I am angry and I write the letter.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.410
We mail it in together.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.853
Now the next week I turn on my TV, and

00:01:21.853 --> 00:01:25.374
like magic, my show is back.

00:01:25.374 --> 00:01:30.800
Now, once again,
every day before school I get colors and

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:36.250
bubbles and explosions and
my life is once again amazing.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:43.216
What did I learn as a seven year old?

00:01:43.216 --> 00:01:47.907
Anger ignites action, ignites change.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:52.237
As a young boy, however,
I was always told that anger,

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:56.396
[FOREIGN] in Malay,
is not part of Malaysian culture.

00:01:56.396 --> 00:01:59.871
[FOREIGN], good boys.

00:01:59.871 --> 00:02:05.296
[FOREIGN] Literally being
soft spoken was synonymous

00:02:05.296 --> 00:02:09.733
with being polite, talking back was bad,

00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:15.413
raising your voice was bad,
anger, [FOREIGN] was bad.

00:02:15.413 --> 00:02:20.459
Yet as I grew up,
there are feelings stronger,

00:02:20.459 --> 00:02:26.137
deeper, and
harder to suppress injustice incited,

00:02:26.137 --> 00:02:31.831
indignation, unfairness,
and leashed umbridge.

00:02:31.831 --> 00:02:35.276
Yet growing up in a semi
democracy meant that

00:02:35.276 --> 00:02:38.731
I couldn't fully express these feelings.

00:02:38.731 --> 00:02:43.505
[FOREIGN] yeah, you don't talk so much.

00:02:43.505 --> 00:02:44.952
You talk, okay.

00:02:44.952 --> 00:02:48.155
The government will come for
you, you watch out.

00:02:48.155 --> 00:02:51.576
Warn my parents, my teachers, adults,

00:02:51.576 --> 00:02:55.992
no wonder the government
had never lost an election.

00:02:55.992 --> 00:03:01.850
People were angry, yes, but
people were even more afraid.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.580
My friends, let me ask you this.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:11.610
When was the last time you were truly,
deeply angry?

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.580
And how did you react to it?

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:16.696
Did you embrace it?

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:21.878
Did you let it move you or did you
distance yourself from this feeling?

00:03:21.878 --> 00:03:27.719
I asked you this, because in my
experience at Stanford, and at Harvard,

00:03:27.719 --> 00:03:33.390
I've found that America isn't so
different from Malaysia after all.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:37.208
At business school and
at public policy school,

00:03:37.208 --> 00:03:43.630
there is this reticence, this distance,
this distancing from anger.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:47.275
We the learned are intellectual,

00:03:47.275 --> 00:03:51.303
we're cerebral, we are above this.

00:03:51.303 --> 00:03:56.235
Fury is seen as uncouth wrath, shameful,

00:03:56.235 --> 00:04:01.580
anger, unbecoming, outrage undignified.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.790
Now, I think this is wrong.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:11.536
And this is why I'm telling
you a story about an uncouth,

00:04:11.536 --> 00:04:19.192
unbecoming Andrew, who used anger
to change lives in profound ways.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:26.614
2018, my Prime Minister steals
$4.5 billion from my country.

00:04:28.291 --> 00:04:33.240
The Guardian calls it the world's
largest financial scandal.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:39.861
Your department of justice calls it
the largest kleptocracy case ever.

00:04:39.861 --> 00:04:45.326
His cronies spend our money
partying with Paris Hilton and

00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:50.234
Leonardo DiCaprio,
his stepson spends our money to

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:54.596
fund the Wolf of Wall Street,
that's right.

00:04:54.596 --> 00:04:59.467
These guys stole Malaysian tax
money to make a movie that

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:05.370
glorifies how Wall Street
stole from American investors.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:09.933
You cannot make this up, how dare you?

00:05:09.933 --> 00:05:13.713
$4.5 billion stolen,

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:19.470
Malaysians are livid like never before.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:24.785
My Prime Minister knows that he
cannot suppress our anger any longer.

00:05:24.785 --> 00:05:29.330
So he decides to suppress our votes.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:32.587
The economists proclaims, stop thief,

00:05:32.587 --> 00:05:37.063
Malaysian prime minister is
about to steal an election.

00:05:37.063 --> 00:05:42.804
Financial Times blares, Malaysian
election falls prey to gerrymandering.

00:05:42.804 --> 00:05:50.145
And as if this was not enough, he decides
to hold polling day on a Wednesday,

00:05:50.145 --> 00:05:54.751
midweek not on a weekend,
as is our tradition.

00:05:54.751 --> 00:05:59.315
This is a blatant attempt to stop
urban voters from traveling home to

00:05:59.315 --> 00:06:02.776
their hometowns to vote,
suppressing turnout.

00:06:02.776 --> 00:06:07.528
How dare you?

00:06:07.528 --> 00:06:13.820
Furious, my friends and I decide to act.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:19.119
We found a movement to mobilize votes.

00:06:19.119 --> 00:06:24.092
We call it [FOREIGN],
go back to vote in Malay.

00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:29.664
We ride the pulse of a nation,
we harness the anger of thousands and

00:06:29.664 --> 00:06:32.860
turn it into real, tangible action.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:38.220
We are an overnight success,
[FOREIGN] becomes the top

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:44.067
trending hashtag on Malaysian Twitter,
we are winning.

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:48.946
And then, And then 17,000

00:06:48.946 --> 00:06:54.455
Russian bots attack us,
17,000 Russian bots.

00:06:54.455 --> 00:07:01.766
One month before this, the world had
learned about Cambridge analytical.

00:07:01.766 --> 00:07:05.843
We had seen how Russian
disinformation swayed

00:07:05.843 --> 00:07:09.197
the results of an American Election.

00:07:09.197 --> 00:07:13.548
And against this backdrop
of global outrage and

00:07:13.548 --> 00:07:18.225
global questions around
the future of democracy,

00:07:18.225 --> 00:07:24.330
we wondered what Russian bots were
doing in a Malaysian election.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:29.097
And then the next day,
our friends in high places

00:07:29.097 --> 00:07:33.870
told us that the Secret Service
was watching us.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.310
We didn't know whether this was true,
or what this meant.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:45.202
But if these threats were true,
real or perceived,

00:07:45.202 --> 00:07:48.770
where our lives and liberty at stake.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.655
This is how they get you.

00:07:52.655 --> 00:07:58.230
Intimidated, half of my team
wanted to shut our platform down.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.725
Like so many before us, we were angry.

00:08:03.725 --> 00:08:08.693
Again, we were also afraid, so

00:08:08.693 --> 00:08:12.189
we sat down over zoom.

00:08:12.189 --> 00:08:14.900
We named our fears.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:18.739
We told our stories and
we were honest to ourselves and

00:08:18.739 --> 00:08:21.576
we listened intently, truthfully.

00:08:21.576 --> 00:08:26.100
And yet, I pushed.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:29.840
I challenge my friends
to close their eyes and

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.498
remember why we started
in the first place.

00:08:33.498 --> 00:08:36.710
Remember the $4.5 billion stolen?

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:41.179
Remember the mid day polling
week to suppress turnout,

00:08:41.179 --> 00:08:45.846
remember the gerrymandering,
together we remembered.

00:08:45.846 --> 00:08:52.431
Together we see and
together once again, we chose to fight.

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:57.819
My friends, in 2018, directly

00:08:57.819 --> 00:09:03.783
helped 10,000 voters travel home to vote.

00:09:03.783 --> 00:09:09.327
Indirectly, we energize
online mobilization,

00:09:09.327 --> 00:09:14.750
helping contribute to
an 82% voter turnout.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:21.722
We the people,
kicked out a corrupt Prime Minister.

00:09:21.722 --> 00:09:26.640
We the people were angry,
we took action and we won.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:32.523
My friends, I am so proud,
so proud to be a small part

00:09:32.523 --> 00:09:36.758
of the first regime change
in Malaysian history.

00:09:36.758 --> 00:09:41.726
So proud to help end the reign of
the longest continuously ruling party in

00:09:41.726 --> 00:09:43.360
the democratic world.

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:48.124
Anger ignites action, ignites change.

00:09:50.025 --> 00:09:56.567
Plato tells us that anger can be powerful.

00:09:56.567 --> 00:10:00.774
He calls it thymus,
a special type of anger,

00:10:00.774 --> 00:10:06.311
a deep dissatisfaction,
a spirited zeal that one can use,

00:10:06.311 --> 00:10:11.875
and harness to overcome fear
to turn inaction into action.

00:10:11.875 --> 00:10:18.453
I see thymus in the global
reaction to stand with Ukraine,

00:10:18.453 --> 00:10:23.270
because we must stand up to mad men.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:28.029
I see thymus and the 20 million
Americans who march for George Floyd,

00:10:28.029 --> 00:10:32.040
the largest Civic Movement
in American history.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.982
Because Black Lives Matter,
I see thymus in Hogg and

00:10:35.982 --> 00:10:40.912
Gonzalez who awaken the consciousness
of millions of students as

00:10:40.912 --> 00:10:44.688
a survivor of
the Parkland High School shooting.

00:10:44.688 --> 00:10:49.728
Because we call BS,
I see thymus [FOREIGN] global

00:10:49.728 --> 00:10:55.148
leaders into climate action
because how dare you.

00:10:55.148 --> 00:11:02.383
My friends, there's so
much injustice in this world.

00:11:02.383 --> 00:11:07.034
And sometimes the only way
out is to be still and

00:11:07.034 --> 00:11:10.620
listen to that voice in your heart.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:15.468
That pinch, that fire in your soul.

00:11:15.468 --> 00:11:20.245
When I am angry, I am closer to the truth.

00:11:20.245 --> 00:11:27.047
And when I am still and
listen to this truth and

00:11:27.047 --> 00:11:32.954
let this truth move me, I am powerful.

00:11:32.954 --> 00:11:36.850
Anger ignites action, ignites change.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:43.509
So I ask you this, ladies and gentlemen,

00:11:43.509 --> 00:11:46.560
what are you angry about?

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.653
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:11:49.653 --> 00:11:52.666
[MUSIC]

